---
description: Avoid direct Make command execution by agents
alwaysApply: true
---

# Command Validation

- Do not run `make ...` commands directly unless the user explicitly asks for that exact command.
- Prefer the underlying script, package command, Cargo command, or direct tool command for validation.
- When documenting a Make target, write it as a target reference, not as a command to execute.
- If a Make target must be validated, use a dry-run or equivalent only after confirming it will not be interpreted by Cursor as a file-open action.
- Before reporting validation, state whether it was run through the underlying script or a direct command instead of Make.
